---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
const shared = [
  ["--cwd <path>", "Run against another directory"],
  ["--json", "Machine-readable output"],
  ["--quiet", "Errors only"],
  ["--verbose", "Extra detail"],
];
const release = [
  ["--tag <tag>", "latest tag", "Which release to build"],
  ["--from <tag>", "previous tag", "Compare base"],
  ["--formats <list>", "from config", "For example og,x"],
  ["--templates <list>", "from config", "For example release-hero"],
  ["--themes <dark|light|both>", "brand theme", "Which themes to render"],
  ["--no-copy", "off", "Force deterministic copy, no LLM"],
  ["--out <dir>", "from config", "Output directory"],
  ["--strict", "off", "Exit 2 on any fit warning"],
  ["--dry-run", "off", "Print facts, render nothing"],
  ["--package <path>", "repo root", "Pick a workspace package"],
];
const story = [
  ["--tag <tag>", "latest tag", "Which release to build"],
  ["--format <format>", "portrait", "One size, or all for every supported size"],
  ["--style <style>", "from brand", "minimal, editorial or terminal"],
  ["--theme <dark|light>", "brand theme", "Which theme to render"],
  ["--headline <text>", "from notes", "Override the cover headline"],
  ["--out <dir>", "from config", "Output directory"],
  ["--strict", "off", "Exit 2 on any fit warning"],
  ["--package <path>", "repo root", "Pick a workspace package"],
];
---
<Docs title="CLI reference: Shipseal" description="Every Shipseal command and flag: init, release, story, preview, milestone, bench and doctor." heading="CLI commands">
  <p>Binary: <code>shipseal</code>. Every command accepts the shared flags below.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{shared.map(([f, m]) => <tr><td><code>{f}</code></td><td>{m}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>shipseal init</h2>
  <p>
    Detects the brand, writes <code>.shipseal/brand.json</code> and <code>.shipseal/config.json</code>,
    offers to update <code>.gitignore</code>, and renders one sample card using the brand it just found.
  </p>
  <p>Flags: <code>--yes</code> accepts the detections without prompting, <code>--force</code> overwrites existing files.</p>

  <h2>shipseal release</h2>
  <p>Generates the release pack.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Default</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{release.map(([f, d, m]) => <tr><td><code>{f}</code></td><td>{d}</td><td>{m}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>shipseal story</h2>
  <p>
    Renders a release as an ordered set of pages instead of a single card: a cover, one page per
    change, a code page when the notes contain a snippet, a before and after page when you supply
    two screenshots, and a closing page. The same pages are written as PNGs, as a PDF carousel and
    as a ZIP that also contains the brand file, the config and the manifest.
  </p>
  <p>
    Pages come from the release notes, the same facts the release pack uses. The closing page links
    your release notes rather than printing an install command, because the command depends on your
    package manager and the release may be breaking. Set <code>release.story.upgrade</code> in
    <code>config.json</code> to supply the real instructions, and they are rendered verbatim.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Default</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{story.map(([f, d, m]) => <tr><td><code>{f}</code></td><td>{d}</td><td>{m}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Screenshots are files you already have. Shipseal never captures or generates one: set
    <code>release.story.before</code> and <code>release.story.after</code> to PNG or JPEG paths, or
    leave both unset and the comparison page is skipped.
  </p>

  <h2>shipseal preview</h2>
  <p>
    Starts a local server on 127.0.0.1 so you can try styles, themes, accents, formats and
    headlines against your real release before committing to them. Nothing leaves the machine and
    nothing is posted. The URL carries a one-time token; requests without it are refused.
  </p>
  <p>
    Save writes only your choices, to <code>.shipseal/brand.json</code> and
    <code>.shipseal/config.json</code>. Preview-only choices stay behind: picking a portrait size to
    look at a carousel does not change the formats your release pack renders.
  </p>
  <p>Flags: <code>--tag &lt;tag&gt;</code>, <code>--port &lt;port&gt;</code> (default 4175), <code>--package &lt;path&gt;</code>.</p>

  <h2>shipseal milestone</h2>
  <p>
    Reads the current metric and renders a card for the highest threshold you have crossed. If nothing has
    been crossed it exits 0 with a message and generates nothing.
  </p>
  <p>Flags: <code>--metric &lt;stars|downloads|contributors&gt;</code>, <code>--threshold &lt;n&gt;</code>.</p>

  <h2>shipseal bench</h2>
  <p>Renders benchmark cards from a JSON file. Percentages are computed by code, never written by a model.</p>
  <pre><code>{`{
  "title": "Rendering got faster",
  "metrics": [
    { "label": "Render time", "before": 420, "after": 87, "unit": "ms", "better": "lower" }
  ],
  "note": "vitest bench, M4, 2026-09-10"
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>Flags: <code>--file &lt;path&gt;</code>. A regression is rendered honestly as a regression.</p>

  <h2>shipseal doctor</h2>
  <p>Checks Node, git, shallow clones, the brand file, fonts, the logo, <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> and the renderer.</p>

  <h2>Exit codes</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>0</code></td><td>Success. Warnings allowed unless <code>--strict</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>1</code></td><td>Error: invalid config, missing required fact, render failure</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>2</code></td><td>Fit warnings present and <code>--strict</code> was set</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</Docs>
